# RA2 Engine for Switch: controller remapping.
# Rename this file to keymap.keys (in sdmc:/switch/ra2engine/) and restart the game.
# Buttons you leave out keep their built-in action (see README "Controls").
#
# Buttons: A B X Y L R ZL ZR PLUS MINUS LSTICK RSTICK DUP DDOWN DLEFT DRIGHT
# Values:
#   MOUSE_LEFT / MOUSE_RIGHT      a mouse click at the cursor (hold + move = drag)
#   a key: h, 2, ESC, ENTER, SPACE, HOME, DELETE, F1 ... F12, UP, DOWN, ...
#   a combo: CTRL+1 (make team 1), SHIFT+1, ALT+1 (center on team 1)
#   CTRL, SHIFT, ALT (or LEFT CTRL, RIGHT CTRL ...): held, it adds that modifier to
#     the other buttons (L=CTRL then Y=1 gives Ctrl+1)
#   SIDEBAR: tap to jump the cursor to the build list and back (like R)
#   SIDEBAR_HOLD: hold to put the cursor on the build list, release to go back to the map
#   NONE: the button does nothing; DEFAULT: the built-in action
#
# Handy keys (the PC hotkeys, changeable in Options > Keyboard): h base, p select all
# combat units, t select all of a type, d deploy, s stop, g guard, x scatter,
# k repair, l sell, q w e r sidebar tabs, 1-0 teams, SPACE last radar event
#
# RSTICK_MOUSE=TRUE   the right stick moves the cursor, the left stick scrolls the map
# DPAD_ARROWS=TRUE    the D-pad scrolls the map (R + D-pad still picks teams)

RSTICK_MOUSE=TRUE
DPAD_ARROWS=TRUE
ZR=MOUSE_LEFT
ZL=MOUSE_RIGHT
L=CTRL
Y=1
B=2
X=3
R=h
A=d
PLUS=ESC
